WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.170
- We really need to have a conversation

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.513
in here about judgment.

00:00:03.513 --> 00:00:04.730
(logo whooshes)
(logo clicks)

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.100
The far majority of you
will not go home today

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.510
and start posting more
on Instagram and LinkedIn

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.713
and Facebook and Twitter.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.833
I love when people be like,

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:17.080
Gary, I didn't grow up
with this technology,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.000
I don't get it.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.530
I'm like, that's nice, Sue.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.899
You didn't grow up driving
and you figured it out.

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:24.390
(audience laughs)

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.560
It is very cute

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.680
that you tell me you
didn't grow up with this

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.120
and that's why you don't get it,

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.480
I am wildly smart enough to understand

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.670
that you are bright enough

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:37.490
to spend two hours on
an app to figure it out.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.030
The reason you're not posting or doing

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.626
is 'cause there's insecurity
about what you're gonna say.

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:43.636
(chill upbeat music)

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:44.860
- Yeah!
- Hey!

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.329
- You got your perspective.

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:49.659
(audience cheering)
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:49.659 --> 00:00:51.510
I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.927
(chill RnB hiphop music)

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.120
The fact that we sit here in 2020

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.910
in the maturity of the social
web and these opportunities

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.470
and there are still two
platforms right this second

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:09.050
that requires $0 for you
to start communicating

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:13.180
what you want to happen in the
world I think is remarkable.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.150
That doesn't even take into account

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.350
the fact that Facebook
ads, YouTube pre-rolls,

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.810
this new Spotify ad product
that is gonna have hosts read

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:25.370
live reads like the old
radio game for podcasts,

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.460
Facebook or Twitter.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.290
Twitter's appropriately priced

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.940
but everything else I
just mentioned to you,

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.430
the ads are underpriced.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.980
The cost of spending
$1,000 on these platforms

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.633
to get people to see
something is underpriced.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.070
I really am desperate.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.100
With even the tone and tenor
that I'm bringing to this talk,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.830
I'm desperate for people to
understand how wild this is.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:53.940
I wanna remind everybody,

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.010
for everybody who raised their hand

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.760
in the first group like myself,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.640
the way you built a business
or brought awareness

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.550
if you're 43 and older
in the way we grew up

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.770
was by spending a lot of money.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.000
Ads cost money.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.810
Direct mail, newspaper,
radio ads, television,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:09.653
they cost money.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.630
It was a very high cost
of entry to build brand.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.450
Brand is the whole game.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.720
I think when I analyze what's going on

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.790
in the business world and with people,

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.690
I think most people are transactional.

00:02:25.798 --> 00:02:27.060
How many people here are entrepreneurs?

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.480
Raise your hands.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.900
I believe the majority of
the hands that just went up

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.480
that when I look at the delta
between the ones who've won

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.520
and the ones who won
less than they wanted to,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.880
I put them always in my
mind into two groups.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.140
One group is transactional,

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.873
a.k.a. deeply care about
the money in the short-term,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.970
and the second group is
looking to build brand,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.890
a.k.a. reputation in perpetuity

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.503
and are more concerned about
playing it out in the longterm.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.640
What is exciting for me right
now is that this device,

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.090
this device, the fact from
this young man down and up,

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:14.090
every one of us has a device
in our hand that is a computer

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.970
that is actually more powerful

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.870
than the computer that Ronald Reagan had

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.410
when he was running the free world.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.920
It really is interesting.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.753
It really is.

00:03:22.753 --> 00:03:25.410
I think, again, what I'm
really trying to establish

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.370
in this talk this morning,

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.933
is I don't think people have
quantified the opportunity.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.830
I struggle, regardless of circumstance,

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.970
with people dwelling or complaining

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.460
in a world where the internet is free,

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.790
has no idea who you are, could care less,

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.490
it's right there and it
becomes a game of skill,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.163
not necessarily finances, to actually win.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.340
It's interesting to me.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.173
It's interesting to me

00:03:51.173 --> 00:03:54.730
that you can be in the
retail business overnight

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:58.690
by setting up a Shopify
account which costs nothing

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.500
when that same action to
sell something 30 years ago

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.430
meant that you have to sign
a lease and build out a store

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.950
and rely on the local
traffic that walk by.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.813
It scares me and excites me

00:04:10.813 --> 00:04:13.170
that the biggest music
company in the world, Spotify,

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.660
was built in Sweden by a kid.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.720
And on and on and on,
you've heard every story.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.630
But more importantly, for
every ridiculous story

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.810
we've seen of Instagram or
Facebook or Uber, Spotify,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:29.600
there are hundreds of thousands of stories

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.920
of people with wins
that are micro versions.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.690
I actually think the most unhealthy thing

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.370
in entrepreneurship and opportunity

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.590
is the big stories that everybody
thinks they have to build

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.670
a billion-dollar company.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.470
I think we do not talk enough

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.367
about the practical $150,000 a year,

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:50.340
$300,000 a year, $700,000 a year business

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.270
that you genuinely love what you do

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.400
and you can live your life being
happy and financially sound

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.460
and what the cost of entry
to be able to do that is

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.500
in today's environment,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.430
which, once again, let me say, very slow,

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.340
between putting out a media company,

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.510
if you decide to put that on
a WordPress or Squarespace,

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:13.540
a retail company on the back of a Shopify,

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.910
you could start a radio
show that is global

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.260
on the back of just uploading
something you record

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.930
on your memos on your phone
and upload onto Spotify

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.650
and Apple and SoundCloud.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.673
My friends, distribution is free.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.040
I know it's a nerdy thing.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.980
It's not some big, profound statement

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.520
but let me say it nice and slow.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.823
Distribution is free, it
used to cost a fortune.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.790
Now, what you put inside of it

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.570
is the variable of your success,

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.703
not your financial capabilities
to create the distribution.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.850
I wish we could zoom in.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.560
I literally have goosebumps
on my neck right now.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.003
No, but really, I really do.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.800
I will live my last breath

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.023
trying to get people to
understand, this is remarkable.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.560
This is a game of perspective.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.230
Are you educated or capable of seeing it

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.970
from the lens that I'm
speaking about today,

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:19.710
which is, the barrier
to reach the end person,

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.180
whether you're a financial advisor

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.500
and trying to get to a client,

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.983
whether you sell bow ties.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.420
How about the fact if you wanna be

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.060
a professional football player

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.680
and now there's all these websites

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.780
where you can upload your film

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.840
because the scout didn't
come to your tiny, tiny town,

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.663
and now, you actually can be discovered?

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.220
Everything has changed.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.160
My question and my
dream every time I speak

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.283
is can I get one person in
this room to get their piece?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.760
For me, if you are not
disproportionately happy

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.180
sitting in this room professionally,

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.010
which will trickle into your actual life,

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.130
you have to take a step back

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.760
and understand this perspective.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.900
So, I think we're living

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.890
through the greatest era
ever for opportunity.

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:08.170
I think it's on the back
of the current internet,

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.520
which is wildly visual.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.990
I'm very aware that the audio revolution

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.680
of our society is coming.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.513
What do I mean by that?

00:07:15.513 --> 00:07:17.280
Is how many people here have a Google Home

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.840
or an Alexa in their house?

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.440
Just raise it high, I'm curious.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.210
Raise it high, I want people to see this.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.160
Google and Alexa, look around.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.110
Some real number.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:28.240
Now, granted, most people
are just telling jokes

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.966
with their Alexa or listening to music.

00:07:29.966 --> 00:07:31.210
(audience laughs)

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:34.280
But I wanna remind everybody
that the first killer app

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.560
on the iPhone for the
first year was that app

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.590
that looked like you were
drinking a beer, if you remember.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:44.690
It takes some time for the apps
to catch up to the platform

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:48.110
but we're all very
close to being in an era

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:51.910
where we order a pizza or
where we get our plumber

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:55.440
or how and where we navigate
by talking to a voice device,

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.473
not to our phone.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:01.640
As voice becomes the platform
and less happens on this,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.160
which seems foreign now
because we all live in it,

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.170
but I wanna remind you,
we used to not live in it,

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.670
and I wanna remind everybody
here, technology likes to move.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.480
When, when.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.080
Not if, when you start
doing a lot of things

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.410
that you do on your phone right now

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.130
start happening on a voice device,

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:21.840
it will no longer be visual and written

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:25.140
which will lead to less
opportunity to grab attention

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:27.240
to the current opportunity landscape,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.750
which I'm gonna remind
everybody, is quite remarkable.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.590
Because if you've got a local bakery now

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.030
and you can do a really good job

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.343
on LinkedIn and TikTok for free
or on Instagram with money,

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:43.090
when in a decade, we go
into voice and I say,

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:48.090
Alexa send me six muffins to the office,

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:52.293
Amazon gets to decide which
muffins come to the office.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.230
Now, if you did such a
good job building brand

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:59.640
and I knew about Carol's Muffins,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.060
and I said Alexa, send me six
Carol's Muffins to the office,

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.083
You've now accomplished your task.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.743
I spend 100,000% of my time on brand.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:12.690
I want people to know my name,

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.820
I want people to know the
name of the things I do,

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.123
VaynerMedia, my agency.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.620
When we killed Mr. Peanut yesterday,

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.010
which a lot of you heard
about, that is us doing brand.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:26.500
That makes you think about Planters.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.600
You weren't thinking about it

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.510
prior to what we did yesterday.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.700
We think about it.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.030
It's all brand.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:35.463
And so, I just want you to
get your long tail of it.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.110
And this is what's led me

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.190
to the most interesting
conversations of my career

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.030
because as a businessman,

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.030
I never thought I would
get into categories

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:48.280
like parenting and
insecurities and self-esteem.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.370
But as somebody who just spoke all that

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.580
and has done that pretty much
every day 600 times a day

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.930
on the internet for the last decade,

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.260
it has led me to realize, wait a minute,

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.650
there's the other component
of everything I said.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:04.060
I can show every one of you what to do.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:09.060
I've just sat here and
told you 100%, not 99,

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.750
the two attention arbitrage platforms

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.280
of our society right now.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.060
If every person here went home

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.800
and made five to seven
pictures and videos a day

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.690
on both TikTok and
LinkedIn, within a year,

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:25.632
something good would happen
for the far majority of you.

00:10:25.632 --> 00:10:30.632
99% of you won't post on
either once after this talk.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.523
The question to me became why.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:37.133
That led to the next part.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:39.450
We really need

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.783
to have a conversation
in here about judgment.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.330
The far majority of you
will not go home today

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.740
and start posting more
on Instagram and LinkedIn

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:50.943
and Facebook and Twitter.

00:10:52.281 --> 00:10:53.114
I love when people like,

00:10:53.114 --> 00:10:55.310
Gary, I didn't grow up
with this technology,

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:56.210
I don't get it.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.750
I'm like, that's nice, Sue.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.053
You didn't grow up driving
and you figured it out.

00:11:00.053 --> 00:11:02.630
(audience laughs)

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.400
It is very cute that you tell me

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.900
you didn't grow up with this

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.330
and that's why you don't get it.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.690
I am wildly smart enough to understand

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.270
that you are bright
enough to spend two hours

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:15.720
on an app to figure it out.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.260
The reason you're not posting or doing

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.110
is 'cause there's insecurity
about what you're gonna say.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.950
You go very deep into who's
gonna care what I'm gonna say.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.440
What would I say?

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.640
Who cares what I think?

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.330
Or even worse, the thing that
breaks my heart the most,

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.000
you actually do post something,

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.090
somebody leaves a post that you look ugly

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.763
and you cripple and
fold like a cheap chair.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.940
So, that's what I spend my time right now:

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.150
trying to figure out how
to get people to realize

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.910
that the judgment of others

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.350
has zero actual impact on their lives,

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.370
they have zero context
on your actual life,

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:55.040
and how do I get you to
understand that perspective,

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.710
which would then lead to you speaking?

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.810
And when I say speaking,
let me break this down.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:03.160
Let me take out the
other excuse of why you

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.610
for yourself and your
business aren't posting.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.910
Not everybody is great
on camera, I get that.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.500
Not everybody is so wildly charismatic

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.428
and very good looking, I get it.

00:12:14.428 --> 00:12:17.090
(audience laughs)

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.803
However, on the flip side,
I am incapable of writing.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.200
It's not my natural skill.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.800
I struggle with reading and
writing, it's not my skill.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.870
Plenty of people here
are incredible writers

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.920
and it is an incredible opportunity

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.610
to go write six to 15 sentences together

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:36.790
around the thought on
LinkedIn and hit post.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.860
Others can work in Photoshop
and make a picture.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.650
Others enjoy, I don't.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.310
I was born in the Soviet Union

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:48.050
and grew up in a very
Eastern European household.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:51.510
I think there's eight pictures
of me in my entire youth.

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.680
We didn't take photos, so it
doesn't come natural to me.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.080
On the other hand,
there are people in here

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.991
who took 97 photos on
their iPhone yesterday.

00:12:57.991 --> 00:13:00.400
(attendees laughing)

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.930
There are plenty people here

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.930
who are great at taking photos.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.950
My question here today, my
friends, is very simple.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.600
When are you gonna start talking?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.390
What are you waiting for?

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.150
If you are not communicating,
you don't exist.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.920
I believe that.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.610
If you are not communicating,
you do not exist.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.173
More importantly, communicate
about what you love.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.970
What scares me about the
long tail of the internet

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.470
is I know there's somebody sitting in here

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.677
who's watched every episode of "Friends",

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.140
deeply loves "Friends",

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.180
can't get enough in their own mind

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:39.730
of debating Rachel and
Ross, loved the show,

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:42.080
watched it every night to go to sleep too,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:46.577
and I know they make 49,
62, 88, $103,000 a year

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.870
doing something they don't like.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.570
And I know that if they started a podcast

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:56.990
about "Friends" everyday
when they went home

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:58.590
instead of consuming content

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.770
to escape the fact that
they don't like their job,

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:05.130
if they created content
around the thing they love,

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.473
that after 24, 36, 48 months,

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.260
along could've came Netflix

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.050
and then a sponsor of that podcast

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:18.680
that would allow them to
actually leave that job they hate

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.550
and now be a full-time
"Friends" podcaster.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.710
You don't believe that, I understand that.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.170
That seems like a
far-fetched story to you.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.130
The problem is you don't live my life

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.260
because I wrote a book in
2009 called "Crush It!"

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.950
that laid this out and I get
to live the best life now

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.500
where I get three to six emails a day

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.160
of people that tell me this exact story,

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.218
whether it's about pickles.

00:14:41.218 --> 00:14:43.700
(audience laughs)

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:44.783
People like pickles.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.253
I eat pickles like crazy.

00:14:49.817 --> 00:14:53.430
"Star Trek", E-sports,
don't even get me started

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.263
'cause I still push it a lot

00:14:54.263 --> 00:14:57.010
and people have gone completely
and made real careers now.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.333
Just stuff.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:04.380
I just really, really, really
hope you hear me today,

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.110
whether it's for yourself,

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:09.290
whether you're a top
executive in your organization

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:12.230
and the company still
does direct mail or print

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.670
or still sponsors the town fair

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:16.440
instead of running content and ads

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:17.420
on Instagram and Facebook.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.693
Guys, it's 2020.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:24.130
And don't give me this not in
my town, not in my industry.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.213
I'm watching, your town, your industry.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.330
And so, that's where we're at.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:35.060
The biggest opportunity in
the history of humankind

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.510
to do what you want to do and yet,

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:39.560
you will continue to find reasons not to.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.040
And I think that comes

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.890
under the categories of
self-esteem and self-awareness

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.190
and I think we need to
make those words important

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:49.580
in our society.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.720
You can work hard all you want.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.400
If you're insecure,
you're gonna be vulnerable

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:55.233
'cause the second there's pushback,

00:15:55.233 --> 00:15:57.423
and there's always
pushback in the journey,

00:15:58.730 --> 00:15:59.563
you won't go there.

00:15:59.563 --> 00:16:01.250
So, that's my framework.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.880
Those are the things I think about.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.730
I spend a lot of time thinking about that.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.670
And then, I have a company that helps

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:10.313
Fortune 500 companies navigate that world,

00:16:13.429 --> 00:16:14.590
and I see it every day.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:15.940
Just going back to the Planters thing

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:18.010
'cause I know it's on the radar today,

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.980
there was a real debate
if we could get America

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:23.180
to know that Mr. Peanut was dead

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.000
so that we could run the Super Bowl spot

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.420
that were running during the Super Bowl,

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:29.643
and if we couldn't, the
spot won't make any sense.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:34.080
I and VaynerMedia knew
that the internet is real.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.847
We knew that if you went on
Twitter, like we did yesterday,

00:16:36.847 --> 00:16:38.780
"The Daily Show" will pick it up at night

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.500
and it will be on all the
recap emails this morning

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:44.810
and in the papers and the
AP and the "USA Today".

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.063
The internet is real
life, this is fake life.

00:16:48.005 --> 00:16:50.838
(audience laughs)

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.740
I know where the giggles come from.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.839
And by the way,

00:16:55.839 --> 00:16:58.189
an enormous amount of
people hate that thought.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:00.740
I live in life.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.250
I know how we are doing such a great job

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.423
currently demonizing technology.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:10.960
My favorite is my friends
who are parents who,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.530
'cause they know where I sit on tech,

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.860
and they're like, Gary,

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.120
I'll be hanging out with
them and they'll be like,

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:18.620
Gary, this tech is terrible,
my kids are on it too much.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.170
But the second the kid comes over

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:24.230
and bothers our conversation
over a glass of wine,

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.890
they throw the iPad at that kid

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.965
like it's the cure to every disease.

00:17:27.965 --> 00:17:30.610
(audience laughs)

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.980
The hypocrisy that we have
around technology is fascinating.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:37.360
We, as humans, are incredible

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.793
at romancing the past and
demonizing the current.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:44.930
And so, these are trends I watch.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:47.130
But I will say this.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:52.130
If you are a vibrant, active,
ambitious human being,

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.610
which there is zero reason for you

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:57.233
to be at this conference
if you're not, zero,

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:02.990
and you do not, for
yourself, or your company,

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.240
produce in the ballpark

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.970
of seven to 25 different pieces of content

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:15.440
across three to nine
different platforms a day,

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.330
you are making a fundamental mistake.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.870
And I'm gonna say it again

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:23.210
because when you're talking
about 25 pieces of content a day

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.220
in a world where 98% of this room

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:28.740
is not making 25 pieces of content a year,

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:30.430
we have a very big disconnect

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:33.733
between where I sit on this
and where you sit on this.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:39.210
I am giving this talk for one reason.

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:43.240
Because D Rock is filming
it, and I'm gonna air it,

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.090
in a decade on whatever
the current platform is

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.740
when it has been completely accepted

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.775
that everything I just
said was 100% right.

00:18:50.775 --> 00:18:52.390
(audience laughs)

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:54.920
I have zero interest

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.463
of you actually taking
the advice I just shared.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:01.722
I don't know you, I've
got my own problems,

00:19:01.722 --> 00:19:03.952
(audience laughs)

00:19:03.952 --> 00:19:04.983
I prefer it.

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.873
I'm speaking at Harvard tomorrow,

00:19:10.078 --> 00:19:10.960
I have a couple of meetings there,

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.610
I gotta go Dallas to Boston,

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.020
land at 1:40 in the morning,

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.650
and then those kinda flights,

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.390
I like reading the emails of you saying,

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.270
hey, I saw you in Mobil in 2020,

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.830
it's now imaginary 2023,

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:26.640
I finally listened, I was
passionate about X, Y and Z,

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.320
I did do an Instagram account

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.920
or a podcast or a YouTube show,

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.220
and now, three years later, this happened.

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:34.600
I love that.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.600
That is the big win for me in this room.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.433
But you won't.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:42.850
You won't.

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:46.630
And I know that 'cause I've
lived this life now for a while.

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:47.500
What is more likely

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.520
is you're gonna email
me in six years and say,

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:52.130
I wish I did 'cause this happened,

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:54.140
because I was the leading lawyer in town

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.740
and this other person who didn't.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.260
The emails are funny, right?

00:19:58.260 --> 00:19:59.960
I mean, they come in all shapes and forms.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:01.557
Gary, I wish I listened to you.

00:20:01.557 --> 00:20:03.030
And you start reading it 'cause I read

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:05.403
'cause I want the qualitative
feedback to learn.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:09.180
Heard you four years ago at
the Atlanta Business Summit.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.540
You said the thing.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.373
I didn't believe you,

00:20:11.373 --> 00:20:13.000
I thought you were loud and obnoxious.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.950
I'm not cursing today
because Maggie asked me,

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:16.635
but, you cursed, it turned me off.

00:20:16.635 --> 00:20:18.710
(audience laughs)

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:19.733
I'm a Jersey boy.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.610
Meanwhile, this upstart
kid, he listened to you,

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.290
and then my favorite line,

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.580
no matter what it is,
lawyer, doctor, real estate,

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:33.500
but, he's not even good at being a lawyer

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.840
but he's killing it on Facebook

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:35.890
and he's hurting my business.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:37.380
What do I do now?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.430
And I smile.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.580
I smile the same way that
I saw some of the kids

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.640
on the field yesterday that
didn't go with VaynerSports

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.410
that we know we were in
the final two with them

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:47.880
and they went in a different direction.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.350
I see them, I root for them.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.720
I'm a kind person, my mom did a good job.

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.210
But I'd be lying to you if I didn't say

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:54.090
when I look at their faces,

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.623
I smile knowing they
made the wrong decision.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.160
'Cause I love merit.

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.680
I love sports.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.240
You either make the
right move or you don't.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:06.330
I've already won by articulating
my thoughts here today.

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:08.700
Either you're gonna actually use this talk

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.410
as the final piece to
actually get out there

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.730
and finally do this because
you cannot be in this room

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:15.840
and not know what I'm
saying is actually right.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:18.640
Or you're not and then you lose

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:20.960
and then I get to see you
'cause they're both good.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.600
I did it or I didn't do it,

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:26.120
I both enjoy 'cause I actually
love the merit of the game.

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:27.100
I mean that.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:30.053
So, I hope you do it.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:33.690
I don't need you to do it.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:36.140
As a matter of fact, I'll
get really technical on you.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:39.950
A lot of my smartest friends
always ask me why I do this

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:43.360
because if these people
start making content

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.480
and start running ads,

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.590
it's gonna be harder for you to build

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.890
what you're building,
Gary, and they're right.

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:54.450
The feed of Instagram, Facebook, Twitter,

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:56.160
it's just one feed.

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.060
It's just supply and demand.

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:00.370
If all of you start posting,

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.603
that's just more content, less attention,

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:06.893
less opportunity for me to
build what I'm building.

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.153
That's where it's going.

00:22:09.153 --> 00:22:13.223
So, I hope I've articulated the punchline.

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.560
I don't think I'm supposed
to be doing Q and A now

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:20.820
but to be very frank, I
gave Maggie the no cursing.

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:21.790
I'm taking the Q and A.

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:23.498
So I'm gonna take a couple
of your questions right now.

00:22:23.498 --> 00:22:27.165
(audience laughs and claps)

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:34.450
Because to be frank, I think
I've articulated my point.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.963
And it is the point.

00:22:38.823 --> 00:22:39.840
I was a terrible student

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:41.390
but there was one class I was decent at,

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:42.580
it was called history.

00:22:42.580 --> 00:22:44.200
And I finally figured out why.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.610
I like history 'cause I know
that things repeat themselves

00:22:46.610 --> 00:22:49.920
and humans are consistent,
and I like context.

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:52.630
If you listen to my talk right
now and immediately ran home

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:55.810
and read a book or articles
about the transition of America

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:57.560
from the radio to the television,

00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.760
everything I just said
would make sense to you.

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:01.630
My friends, we have transitioned

00:23:01.630 --> 00:23:04.470
from the newspaper and
television to the internet.

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:05.490
It's happened.

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:07.433
It's not going back, I'm sorry.

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:09.675
It's not my fault.

00:23:09.675 --> 00:23:11.000
(audience laughs)

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.320
It has happened.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.160
It's never going back.

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:15.960
This is why the mainstream media

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.620
will always be wrong
about their predictions

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:19.720
'cause they look at the wrong data.

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:21.420
They will always be wrong.

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:22.370
Watch it again.

00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:24.310
They'll always be wrong.

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:25.660
It's like, big companies,

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:26.900
why my company's exploding

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.360
because they worked with other agencies

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:30.970
for the "Mad Men" era,
they're always wrong.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:34.373
It's based on subjectivity, politics, ego.

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:37.430
We're here.

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:39.160
I want you to take advantage of it

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:41.750
'cause if you don't, somebody else will.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:45.670
There's 330 million of us
out here in this country,

00:23:45.670 --> 00:23:46.690
and 7.7 billion.

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:47.523
Yes, sir.

00:23:47.523 --> 00:23:50.360
- [Brent] Yeah, so, Gary, as
a person that runs a company--

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.298
- What's your name?

00:23:51.298 --> 00:23:52.160
- [Brent] My name is Brent.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:52.993
- Brent?
- Yeah.

00:23:52.993 --> 00:23:54.100
- Nice to meet you.

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:55.623
- For a person who runs a company,

00:23:55.623 --> 00:23:56.470
and we have first ads

00:23:56.470 --> 00:23:58.710
on our social media platforms accounts.

00:23:58.710 --> 00:24:00.170
- The company?
- I have one for--

00:24:00.170 --> 00:24:01.544
- [Gary] They're personal.

00:24:01.544 --> 00:24:02.934
- Yeah, for their business,

00:24:02.934 --> 00:24:04.646
how do you divide up content?

00:24:04.646 --> 00:24:06.300
Do you cross-pollinate there?
- Yes.

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:07.347
- What would you
recommended to the person?

00:24:07.347 --> 00:24:09.180
- Brent, I think you can do both.

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:10.013
I do.

00:24:10.013 --> 00:24:11.590
I'm Gary Vee but my family wine business,

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.620
Wine Library has an account.

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:13.453
Empathy Wines,

00:24:13.453 --> 00:24:15.730
my direct-to-consumer
wine brand has an account,

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.810
VaynerMedia has an account.

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.300
We cross-pollinate.

00:24:19.300 --> 00:24:21.830
Obviously, if you're a big personality,

